"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[806],{6039(e,o,t){t.r(o),t.d(o,{_pageData:()=>r,default:()=>s});var a=t(641);const r=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-pre-order/installation.html","title":"Installation & Plugin Updates","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-pre-order/installation.md"}'),n={name:"installation.md"},s=(0,t(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,o,t,r,n,s){return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[...o[0]||(o[0]=[(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="installation-plugin-updates" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#installation-plugin-updates"><span>Installation &amp; Plugin Updates</span></a></h1><p>Learn how to download, install, configure, and safely update the WooCommerce Pre-Order plugin on your WordPress site.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-installation-via-wordpress-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-installation-via-wordpress-dashboard"><span>1. Installation via WordPress Dashboard</span></a></h2><p>This is the recommended and easiest installation method:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Download the ZIP File:</strong> Log into your Webkul account and download the <code>wp-woocommerce-pre-order</code> plugin ZIP file.</p></li><li><p><strong>Navigate to Plugins:</strong> Log into your WordPress admin panel and go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Add New</strong>. <img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/installation-add-new.png" alt="Navigate to Plugins and Add New"></p></li><li><p><strong>Upload the Plugin:</strong> Click <strong>Upload Plugin</strong> at the top. Choose the downloaded ZIP file and click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/installation-choose-file.png" alt="Choose ZIP File"></p></li><li><p><strong>Activate:</strong> Once the upload completes, click <strong>Activate Plugin</strong>.</p></li></ol><hr><h2 id="_2-installation-via-ftp-sftp" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-installation-via-ftp-sftp"><span>2. Installation via FTP / SFTP</span></a></h2><p>If you experience server upload limits, upload the plugin files directly:</p><ol><li><strong>Extract the ZIP File:</strong> Extract the downloaded <code>wp-woocommerce-pre-order.zip</code> on your local computer. This creates a folder named <code>wp-woocommerce-pre-order</code>.</li><li><strong>Connect to your Server:</strong> Use an FTP client (such as FileZilla) to connect to your web host.</li><li><strong>Upload the Folder:</strong> Navigate to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> and upload the extracted <code>wp-woocommerce-pre-order</code> folder.</li><li><strong>Activate:</strong> Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Installed Plugins</strong> in your WordPress dashboard, find &quot;WooCommerce Pre-Order&quot;, and click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="_3-module-translation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-module-translation"><span>3. Module Translation</span></a></h2><p>The WooCommerce Pre-Order plugin is localization-ready and can be translated into any language. Follow these steps to translate the interface:</p><ol><li><strong>Locate translation template:</strong> The translation template file (<code>.pot</code>) is located in the plugin&#39;s <code>/languages/</code> directory.</li><li><strong>Use Translation Tool:</strong> Open the <code>.pot</code> template file using a tool like <strong>Poedit</strong> or the <strong>Loco Translate</strong> plugin.</li><li><strong>Translate Strings:</strong> Translate the source strings to your target language.</li><li><strong>Save Files:</strong> Save the translation files with the correct locale extension: <ul><li><code>.po</code> file (e.g., <code>woocommerce-pre-order-fr_FR.po</code> for French)</li><li><code>.mo</code> compiled translation file (e.g., <code>woocommerce-pre-order-fr_FR.mo</code>)</li></ul></li><li><strong>Deployment Path:</strong> Upload the saved <code>.po</code> and <code>.mo</code> files to the standard WordPress languages directory:<div class="language-text line-numbers-mode" data-highlighter="prismjs" data-ext="text"><pre><code class="language-text"><span class="line">/wp-content/languages/plugins/</span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true" style="counter-reset:line-number 0;"><div class="line-number"></div></div></div>This ensures that translation files are not overwritten when you update the plugin.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="_4-module-activation-license-verification" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-module-activation-license-verification"><span>4. Module Activation &amp; License Verification</span></a></h2><p>To receive plugin updates and customer support directly inside your WordPress dashboard, activate your plugin license:</p><ol><li><strong>Navigate to License Settings:</strong> Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Webkul License Manager</strong> or find the license activation tab in your plugin settings.</li><li><strong>Provide Credentials:</strong><ul><li><strong>Purchase Code:</strong> Copy the unique purchase key from your Envato/Webkul account.</li><li><strong>Registered Email:</strong> Enter the email address used during purchase.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Activate:</strong> Click <strong>Activate License</strong>. A green success badge indicates successful verification.</li></ol><p>For a detailed step-by-step walkthrough, please refer to the <a href="https://wpdoc.webkul.com/license-validator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Webkul License Validator Guide</a>.</p><hr><h2 id="_5-safe-update-procedures" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-safe-update-procedures"><span>5. Safe Update Procedures</span></a></h2><p>Webkul regularly releases updates containing features, bug fixes, and performance improvements. Follow these guidelines to update safely:</p><h3 id="data-safety" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#data-safety"><span>Data Safety</span></a></h3><p>All pre-order campaigns, subscriber lists, settings, and transaction records are stored securely in your website&#39;s database. <strong>Deleting the plugin files will not delete your pre-order configurations or customer history.</strong></p><blockquote><p>[!WARNING] Before performing any plugin updates, always take a complete backup of your database.</p></blockquote><h3 id="update-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#update-workflow"><span>Update Workflow:</span></a></h3><ol><li>Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Installed Plugins</strong>.</li><li>Find <strong>WooCommerce Pre-Order</strong> and click <strong>Deactivate</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Delete</strong> to remove the old version files (your database data remains safe).</li><li>Upload the new version ZIP file via <strong>Plugins</strong> &gt; <strong>Add New</strong> &gt; <strong>Upload Plugin</strong>.</li><li>Click <strong>Activate Plugin</strong>. The plugin will automatically run migration checks and apply database updates if required.</li></ol>',27)])])}]])}}]);